;;; `ein solve --dump-answer` refused a `.einb` — **W43**, register row
;;; `W43/einb-dump-answer` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two names, `a` and `b`, each seen, and `p` the relation a run may commit
;;; to: the candidates are `(p a)` and `(p b)`. One rule, `clash`, refutes the
;;; two together. So R is three states, ∅, {(p a)} and {(p b)}, and N is one
;;; set, {(p a), (p b)}, whose core is the two facts, refuted by `clash`: an
;;; answer directory with state files and a member of N with its core.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Every command that takes a `.ein` path takes a `.einb` too, dispatching on
;;; the magic bytes (`docs/ein/ein.rs/design/binary-format.md`), and no two
;;; commands, or one command on two forms of one program, may disagree
;;; (Q-M1e2.32). A `.einb` stores its program, resolved and
;;; import-flattened, and every command reads it (W40's six rows), so `ein
;;; solve x.einb --dump-answer DIR` answers as `ein solve x.ein --dump-answer
;;; DIR` does (Q-M1f.27): exit 0, R's three states on stdout, and `DIR` holding
;;; a state file for each, the stored program and then the state, and
;;; `nogoods.json` with N's one member, its core (p a) (p b) and its rule, `clash`.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answers ────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The right answer: the dump writes every file from the program the
;;; container stores. The engine had `ein solve` refuse the container before
;;; the run, exit 2, with `error: --dump-answer DIR: a .einb container carries
;;; no program source, and every file the answer directory holds starts with
;;; it — run it on the .ein`, where `ein solve` on the container without
;;; `--dump-answer`, and every other command, answered it.
;;;
;;;

(relation p T :why "{?1} is picked")
(relation seen T :why "{?1} is seen")

(seen a)
(seen b)

(rule clash () :match (and (p a) (p b)) :assert (false)
  :why "a and b are not both picked")

(solve :hypothesis-relations (p))
